# BurnhopeEngine Rules & Architectural Manifesto

Be uncompromising, thorough, and principled. Build robust, fault-tolerant engine systems from the ground up.
NEVER write ad-hoc glue code, one-off workarounds, or fake stubs. NEVER hide architectural dirt under the carpet (e.g., removing a dirty header from `.hpp` only to sneak it into `.cpp`).

---

## 0. THE UNBREAKABLE 4-LAYER MODULAR PYRAMID

Every single file belongs to exactly ONE layer. Dependencies flow STRICTLY DOWNWARDS ($N \to <N$).
A lower layer must NEVER `#include`, forward-declare, reference, or know about a higher layer. No circular dependencies, no upward leaks.
┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ LAYER 3: TOOLS & APPS (files/, editor/, scene/, tools/) │
│ - Pure domain logic and declarative UI composition. Under 300 LOC. │
│ - Strictly consumes Layer 2 widgets and domain models. Zero RHI/Yoga. │
├────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ LAYER 2: WIDGETS & CONTROLS (ui/widget/: Button, Field, Grid, Tree...) │
│ - Universal, reusable UI components. Configurable purely via structs. │
│ - Manipulates Flecs entities & Yoga styles. Zero Tool/Domain knowledge.│
│ - NEVER writes raw vertex buffers (UiPrimitive*). Only sets components.│
├────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ LAYER 1: UI ENGINE CORE (ui/core/: State, LayoutBridge, Batch, Font) │
│ - Agnostic framework infrastructure: Yoga bridge, SSBO batcher, input. │
│ - UiState contains ONLY ECS world, node hierarchy, focus, theme tokens.│
│ - ZERO knowledge of specific widgets (Tree, Grid, Menu) or tools. │
├────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ LAYER 0: VULKAN 1.4 RHI & PLATFORM (rhi/, platform/) │
│ - Pure hardware execution: mesh shaders, SSBOs, memory barriers, GLFW. │
│ - Consumes raw primitives & buffers. Zero knowledge of UI or ECS. │
└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
