---

## 1. ANTI-LAZINESS & REFACTORING PROTOCOL (NO SHORTCUTS)
- **NEVER DELETE FEATURES TO MAKE CODE SHORTER**: When refactoring, ALL functionality (context menus, inline F2 rename, rubberband selection, Ctrl/Shift modifiers, hierarchy chevrons, forward/back history) MUST be preserved by moving logic into proper Layer 2 widgets, NEVER by stripping code.
- **NEVER FAKE WIDGETS WITH HARDCODED ARRAYS**: BANNED: `wTree[12]`, `wCell[18]`, `crumbs.seg[8]`, `pop.row[12]`. ALWAYS use dynamic virtual recycling (`UiVirtualPool`, `kUiPoolCap`).
- **NEVER BIND CORE TO DEMO LOGIC**: BANNED: hardcoded strings (`"list_inner"`, `"status"`), hardcoded slots, or demo drag-reordering in `Input.cpp`, `Tree.cpp`, or `List.cpp`.
- **NO PHANTOM LABELS**: Controls (Button, Check, Field) are single Flecs entities that own their `UiText` and `UiPaint`. NEVER spawn a child `Label` entity in `spawn()` and hack its bounding box via `placeChromeText` / `fieldPlaceText`.
- **HEADER HYGIENE**: BANNED: monolithic mega-headers like `Detail.hpp` including all 16 widget headers. Every file includes ONLY the headers it directly consumes.

---

## 2. Core Architecture, C++26 & Data-Oriented Design
- **Language**: Strict C++26. Pure Data-Oriented Design (DOD). AVX2 desktop PC only (Linux & Windows x86_64). Zero support for mobile, web, or legacy OS.
- **ECS (Flecs)**: Query archetype column pointers (`flecs::column<T>`). NEVER call `entity.get<T>()` / `try_get<T>()` in hot loops.
- **COMPONENT OVER TAG**: NEVER use negative magic tags (`-5, -6, -7, -15, -90`) to identify widgets in `Input.cpp` or batching; ALWAYS use dedicated Flecs components (`UiSplitter`, `UiTitleBar`, `UiMenuBar`, `UiResizable`, `UiImage`).
- **Hot-Path Allocations**: ZERO heap allocations in `Tick`, `Layout`, `Emit`, `Draw`. NO `malloc`, `new`, `std::string`, `push_back`, or `std::make_shared`. Use bump allocators, ring buffers, or `FrameArena`.
- **POD Invariants**: All GPU and UI data must be trivially copyable POD types (`sizeof % 16 == 0`).
- **Fault-Tolerance**: Bounds-checked arrays only. File parsers (JSON, Binary) must NEVER infinite-loop on syntax errors or mock fake fallback UI cards on read errors (`kFallback` is banned).

---

## 3. UI Framework & Rendering Architecture
- **Layered Structure**: Base components (Button, Label, Scroll, Icon) sit directly on Layer 1 Core. Composite tools (Explorer, Inspector) sit strictly in Layer 3.
- **BANNED UI**: Absolutely NO ImGui, NO Qt (`QObject`, MOC, virtual dispatch hierarchies), NO legacy immediate-mode GUI hacks.
- **Draw Submission**: Single `vkCmdDraw` / `vkCmdDrawMeshTasksEXT` call per frame from mapped host-visible SSBO ring buffer.
- **Virtual Scrolling (DRY)**: NEVER duplicate scroll math across `Scroll.cpp`, `Virtual.cpp`, `VirtualGrid.cpp`, `TreeView.cpp`; ALWAYS route content height and recycling via `UiVirtualPool`.
- **Text & Word-Wrapping (DRY)**: Unified text measurement and line-breaking (`uiWrapCut`) for both labels and text fields.
- **Design System Invariants**: NEVER paint widget chrome with raw RGB floats (`0.14f, 0.15f, 0.18f`); ALWAYS use `paintToken` / `UiToken` so theme switches apply globally.
- **Layout Invariants**:
  - NEVER place `uiSlider` with 100% width in horizontal row next to a label (Yoga collapses box to 0). Stack vertically.
  - Role `Scroll` requires `UiScroll.inner`.
  - Absolute coordinates in `cacheBox` must be computed hierarchically in $O(1)$ from parent bounds, NEVER by climbing ancestors up to the root.
  - `uiLayout` must be $O(N)$, inspecting flex drop victims directly via Yoga children without $O(N^2)$ full-tree rescans.
- **Scissor Discipline**: Every container strictly routes clipping through the core scissor manager so text and geometry never leak into neighboring panels.

---

## 4. Vulkan 1.4 & Next-Gen Graphics Pipeline
- **Modern Standards REQUIRED**:
  - GPU-Driven pipeline via Mesh Shaders (`VK_EXT_mesh_shader`, meshlets).
  - Dynamic Rendering (`vkCmdBeginRendering` / `vkCmdEndRendering`) with no render pass boilerplate.
  - Shader Objects (`VK_EXT_shader_object` + `vkCmdBindShadersEXT`).
  - Bindless descriptors via `VK_EXT_descriptor_heap` and Buffer Device Address (BDA).
  - Synchronization2 (`vkCmdPipelineBarrier2`), Timeline Semaphores, Host Image Copy.
  - Lighting & GI: Radiance Cascades (RC), clustered light grids, two-phase GPU Hi-Z culling.
- **BANNED Legacy Vulkan**:
  - NEVER use `VkRenderPass`, `VkFramebuffer`, or runtime `VkPipeline`.
  - NEVER use classic descriptor sets/pools (`VkDescriptorSet`), `vkCmdPipelineBarrier` (v1), or binary fences per pass.
  - NEVER call `vkDeviceWaitIdle` or block CPU fences inside the frame loop.
  - NEVER use `VK_KHR_mesh_shader` (use `VK_EXT_mesh_shader`).
  - NEVER write per-dispatch constants via `vkCmdUpdateBuffer`.
- **Submission Contract**: Scene finishes on color after `LOAD_CLEAR` and signals only `uiSem`. Canvas waits `uiSem`, runs `LOAD`, transitions to `PRESENT_SRC`, and signals present. Scene never calls `swapchainToPresent`.

---

## 5. Memory Slots & Uniform Invariants
- `GizmoGpu` uniform MUST be 320 bytes (multiple of 64).
- `FrameView` is 384 bytes (binding 0). `FrameSun` is 1920 bytes (binding 49, slot `HeapBuf::Sun`). Slider blocks: bindings 50–57 (64 bytes each).
- Canvas primitives strictly own buffer slot 22 (`kUiDescPrims`). Font is 661; UI photos are 662–669. NEVER overwrite slot 22 with render passes (RC hash uses slot 18).
- Shared shader math lives exclusively in `engine/shader/core/` and `camera.slang`. Never duplicate math across passes.

---

## 6. Self-Maintenance Protocol & Mandatory Verification
- **MANDATORY BUILD & TEST**: After making edits, ALWAYS verify both targets:
  `cmake --build build-core --target BurnhopeTest BurnhopeEngine -j && ./build-core/BurnhopeTest`
  Task is COMPLETE ONLY if BOTH targets compile cleanly and all unit tests pass.
- **NO TERMINAL SPAM**: Do not run `git diff` or cat whole files into chat via shell. Output clear, direct code modifications.
- When resolving an architectural bug, ban it directly:
  `- NEVER [banned API/action] (causes [technical failure]); ALWAYS [modern alternative] [exact slots/bytes/alignment].`
- Keep exact technical contracts only. Keep this file under 160 lines.